    "summary": "Adire cloth: composed of four uneven lengths of machine plain woven European cotton machine sewn together . The textile is decorated using the tie-dyed method. The producer has tied the desired pattern into the textile before dyeing the textile indigo.  The pattern is composed of nine regularly spaced spirals on a background of small circles. This pattern is called AKETE or the &#039;Caps.&#039;  The hem is machine sewn.",
